comments.body:
PR #952 is now open: https://github.com/gazebosim/ros_gz/pull/952

Additional validation on the current `ros2` branch before opening the PR:

- the four-file patch applied cleanly to the ordinary user workspace while preserving two unrelated pre-existing CMake edits, and `ros_gz_bridge` built successfully;
- all 73 generated topic mapping pairs were instantiated in both directions;
- generated payload assertions passed 73/73 for GZ→ROS and 73/73 for an ordered ROS→GZ run;
- the ordered 73-pair ROS→GZ run shut `parameter_bridge` down with exit 0 and no escalation;
- five repeated payload runs and eleven lifecycle-only runs also exited cleanly.

The stock macOS launch-test harness still has separate startup-order and test-helper teardown failures. They are recorded as limitations rather than attributed to this ownership patch.
